1
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:06,640
Modern Times has been a hub for Minneapolis through many national events.

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:11,600
It's just blocks away from the sites of several high-profile incidents over the past few years,

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:15,380
including the deaths of George Floyd, Rene Good, and Alex Preddy.

4
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:18,460
Owner Dylan Alverson says the idea is simple.

5
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:21,880
By operating on donations and not generating sales tax,

6
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:26,600
the cafe won't be contributing to what he calls the armed occupation of the city.

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:31,480
Alverson says it's a reflection of the city and the country that, in his words,

8
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:34,340
is in chaos and local business must adapt.

9
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,840
People are hiding. People are living under trauma.

10
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,960
People can't afford to eat at restaurants even before this.

11
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:46,500
And it was something that I wanted to provide for anyone in the city right now,

12
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,080
whether their economic status or, I guess, time management.

13
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:56,380
People out patrolling blocks and helping their neighbors and all these things.

14
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:58,180
People forget to eat. I forget to eat.

15
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,840
Now, look at this pie over here. Look how big this is.

16
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:02,860
This is like you get this at grandma's house.

17
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:06,200
This is beautiful. I'm going to take a bite of this.

18
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:08,020
It's focaccia style.

19
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,180
You've got, like, a sweet tomato sauce.

20
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,260
I can say, are you using San Marzano tomatoes over here?

21
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:12,760
Yes.

22
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,960
What kind of cheese? Is this grande mozzarella or no?

23
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:17,220
This is actually a local provolone.

24
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:20,980
Oh, I love provolone. It's sharper. This is my style.

25
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,260
I'm going to be hanging out at this cafe.

26
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:26,860
So why did you decide to exclude federal agents from the free menu?

27
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,440
They're perpetrating violence on our community.

28
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:35,400
They're killing our neighbors, our customers, our friends.

29
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:38,260
I've witnessed firsthand their brutality.

30
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:41,080
I've been tear gassed several times the last week.

31
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:47,800
My wife was shot in the face with a pepper ball standing on Nicollet Avenue.

32
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:58,760
I guess I, you know, if there's anyone in this neighborhood that we hear about that's committing crimes against people or terrorizing people, I'm not going to serve them.

33
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:07,220
Regular patrons say they're inspired by the new approach, with some already leaving donations on Venmo or in person, showing solidarity with the restaurant and the community.

34
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:13,740
They are very clear about not accepting ice in this cafe, and that in itself is political.

35
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:18,360
I think it's a community effort because they're offering free food when they do not have to.

36
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:22,940
And there was no guarantee that they were going to make that money back throughout donations.

37
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:30,920
But not only are they in some way relying on their community, they put a lot of faith in their community.

38
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,700
Um, and they're putting in a lot of love out there.

39
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:42,140
Just the amount of love and support we've received over the last couple days has been quite amazing.

40
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:47,680
Like, I'm getting DMs from people over in, like, Paris, France that are doing, like, a pop-up for us.

41
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:53,220
Like, they're donating, like, all of their proceeds from the entire night to us, and it's like, that's, like, amazing.

42
00:02:53,220 --> 00:03:03,600
For now, Postmodern Times is open daily from 9am to 3pm, hoping to make a statement about community, safety, and resistance in a town that has become the epicenter for all the protests nationally.

